<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's inflation 2.04 pct in April.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's inflation 2.04 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Consumer Price Index rose by 2.04 percent in April, up from a 2.83 percent rise during the same month last year, the National Statistics and Census Institute said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Annual inflation was 28.91 percent in April.</p>
<p>In March, consumer prices rose by 1.46 percent.</p>
<p>The government expects to close 1997 with an inflation rate of around 30 percent.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
